{
  "A panel that comes up from the bottom of the page or of a container and stops at a few heights: a peek, half, full, as tall as its content, or heights of your own. Dragged by its handle and its title, flicked, swiped down to close; modal or not, with the browser's back closing it on a phone.": "",
  "In JSX, `x-model` opens and closes it with the state. Programmatically, `show(host)` puts it in a component and disposes it when it closes; `open()` and `close()` work on one that stays. Without a `container` it opens over the whole page, in the browser's top layer.": "",
  "Heights, dragging and options": "",
  "`detents` are the heights it stops at, `detent` the one it is at. The handle and the title follow the finger and the mouse; the content takes the sheet along from its top. Here it opens over a frame (`container`), not modal, so the page under it stays usable. Every behaviour is a switch, live.": "",
  "Each opening, closing and change of height asks first and reports after. `onClosing` tells why (`reason`) and can keep it open; `onDetentChanging` can refuse a height or pick another.": "",
  "Closes it (`closeOnEscape`).": "",
  "The next taller height.": "",
  "The next lower height; it does not close it.": "",
  "The lowest and the tallest height.": "",
  "Finger and mouse": "",
  "The sheet follows the finger or the mouse; let go, it goes to the nearest height. Past the tallest it gives a little.": "",
  "Faster than `flickSpeed`: on to the next height that way, however far it went.": "",
  "It closes (`swipeToClose`), with `reason: 'swipe'`.": "",
  "Down from its top, or up while the sheet is not at its tallest, the sheet moves; otherwise the content scrolls. A sideways swipe is the content's.": "",
  "The next height, round to the lowest.": "",
  "The panel is `role=\"dialog\"`, named by its title (else `label`, else \"Sheet\"), `aria-modal` when modal. What is around it is made `inert`, so screen readers and the keys stay inside.": "",
  "`role=\"slider\"`, vertical, named \"Sheet height\"; its value is the share of the full height, read as the height's name (\"Half height\").": "",
  "Moves in when it opens (modal by default) and back to where it was when it closes.": "",
  "The panel keeps clear of the screen's rounded corners and bars (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`).": "",
  "The handle's name and heights, the default name and the close button come from `uiLocale.strings` (`sheetHandle`, `sheetPeek`, `sheetHalf`, `sheetFull`, `sheetFit`, `sheetHeight`, `sheetLabel`, `close`).": "",
  "The layer over the page or the container. `data-open`, `data-modal`, `data-scrim`, `data-contained`, `data-dragging`.": "",
  "The dimmed layer.": "",
  "The dialog. `--_size` is its height, `--_drop` how far it is pulled below its lowest height.": "",
  "The handle (the slider) and the line drawn in it.": "",
  "The title row and its close button.": "",
  "The content that scrolls, and the row under it.": "",
  "Units: the dimmed layer; the surface (`max-width`: how wide it gets on a large screen; `full`: its top corners once it reaches the top of the room).": "",
  "Units: the handle (`focus`: the keys) and its grip.": "",
  "The gap it leaves at the top at full height, the peek height, the room around the panel.": "",
  "The handle’s grab area; the type’s family.": "",
  "A title at the top; it names the dialog. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "Names it for screen readers when it has no title (else \"Sheet\", from `uiLocale`).": "",
  "The heights it stops at: `'peek'` (`sheet.peek-height`), `'half'`, `'full'` (the room but `sheet.top-gap`), `'fit'` (as tall as its content), pixels, or a share such as `'40%'`.": "",
  "the first of `detents`": "",
  "The height it opens at and is at now; the user moving it writes it, setting it moves the sheet.": "",
  "Nothing around it can be used: inside its container, or on the whole page. Tab stays inside.": "",
  "when modal": "",
  "A dimmed layer under it.": "",
  "Opens over this element (a static one is made relative while it is open); `null` over the page, in the top layer.": "",
  "What fills it, next to JSX children, and a row under it that does not scroll.": "",
  "A close button beside the title.": "",
  "The handle at the top: a grip for the finger and the mouse, a slider for the keys.": "",
  "The finger and the mouse move it between its heights by the handle and the title.": "",
  "A finger on the content takes the sheet along when the content cannot scroll that way: down from its top, up while the sheet is not at its tallest.": "",
  "Dragged or flicked down below its lowest height, it closes.": "",
  "How fast a flick goes on to the next height, in pixels per millisecond.": "",
  "Escape and a press on the scrim close it.": "",
  "The browser's back (Android's back button, the back gesture) closes it: it holds one history entry while open and takes it back when it closes otherwise, so no entry is left behind.": "",
  "Focus moves in when it opens: `[autofocus]`, the first field, the first control, else the panel.": "",
  "Focus goes back where it was when it closes.": "",
  "Disposed when it closes: by default when `show` put it in its host.": "",
  "Opens it at `detent`; `false` when `onOpening` said no. Placed nowhere, it opens from the end of the page (or in its container).": "",
  "Opens or closes it.": "",
  "Adds it to `host` (a component or the application) unless it is placed, and opens it; it is disposed when it closes.": "",
  "Moves it to a height (and opens it there when closed).": "",
  "To the next taller or lower height; `false` at the end.": "",
  "Whether it is open (reactive), and its height now in pixels.": "",
  "The surface with `role=\"dialog\"`, and the area that scrolls.": "",
  "`{ cancel, source }` / `{ source }`; opened comes after it slid in.": "",
  "`{ cancel, reason, source }` / `{ reason, source }`: `'code'`, `'escape'`, `'scrim'`, `'swipe'`, `'back'`, `'button'`, `'owner'`. The owner going away cannot be refused.": "",
  "`{ from, to, byUser, cancel, source }`: `to` can be changed; refused, the sheet goes back where it was.": "",
  "Every prop is a property too, taking a value or a function. The shared parts (the panel, the scrim, modality, focus and the back button) are `OverlayPanel`'s, which `Drawer` and `ActionSheet` build on as well.": ""
}
